-- title:
--   Generator law conjugates ⟨ d⟩ into ⟨ d'⟩ on X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $M\ge 1$ with $p\nmid M$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of level $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta\in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$, and let $j\in K$ have underlying series the image of $q^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNum}$. Let $\sigma$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ subject to the following generator law: there are a ring embedding $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb{C}$ and $\gamma\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M)$ and $p\mid\gamma_{11}$ such that for every weight $k$, every pair $f,g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ (that is, $p_f,p_g\in\mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ mapping to the $q$-expansions of $f,g$) with the Laurent series of $p_g$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ non-zero, and every $x\in K$ whose underlying series is the image of $p_f/p_g$, there exist modular forms $\varphi_f,\varphi_g$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ and non-zero integers $D_f,D_g$ with $\varphi_f=D_f\cdot\big(\tau\mapsto (f\mid_k\gamma)(p\tau)\big)$ and $\varphi_g=D_g\cdot\big(\tau\mapsto (g\mid_k\gamma)(p\tau)\big)$ pointwise on the upper half-plane (the dilation being by [`ModularForm.heckeDiagMatrix p`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperator.html#L21), the matrix $\mathrm{diag}(p,1)$), such that each of $\varphi_f,\varphi_g$ is a finite $\iota(L)$-linear combination of forms of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ admitting integral $q$-expansions, and, in $\mathbb{C}((q))$, $\iota(\sigma x)\cdot D_f\cdot\widehat{\varphi_g}=D_g\cdot\widehat{\varphi_f}$, where $\widehat{\ \cdot\ }$ denotes the $q$-expansion at width $1$. The conclusion is: for all natural numbers $d,d'$ coprime to $Mp$ with $d'\equiv d$ in $\mathbb{Z}/M$ and $d'd=1$ in $\mathbb{Z}/p$, and for any $L$-algebra automorphisms $\theta_d,\theta_{d'}$ of $K$ which agree, on underlying Laurent series, with the base change to $L$ (via [`ModularCurve.baseChangeAut`](def/ModularCurve_X1Diamond.html#L24)) of the diamond automorphisms [`ModularCurve.diamondAut (M * p) d`](def/ModularCurve_X1Diamond.html#L66) and [`ModularCurve.diamondAut (M * p) d'`](def/ModularCurve_X1Diamond.html#L66) of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$, one has $\sigma\circ\theta_d\circ\sigma^{-1}=\theta_{d'}$, expressed as equality of underlying Laurent series at every $x\in K$. Here `diamondAut N d` is a chosen $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism of the function field characterised by $d$ being coprime to $N$ and by the property that, for all $f,g$ of one weight $k$ on $\Gamma_1(N)$ with integral $q$-expansions and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(N)$ with $\gamma_{00}\equiv d \pmod N$, its value on the ratio of the two $q$-expansions, read in $\mathbb{C}((q))$, times the $\gamma$-slashed expansion of $g$ equals that of $f$ (and the identity if no such automorphism exists); `baseChangeAut` is a chosen extension to the $L$-base change commuting with the coefficient embedding.
--
--   This is the function-field form of the classical relation $w_p\langle d\rangle w_p^{-1}=\langle d'\rangle$ on $X_1(Mp)$ for $d'\equiv d \pmod M$ and $dd'\equiv 1\pmod p$, the partial Atkin–Lehner involution at $p$ inverting the diamond operator modulo $p$ while preserving it modulo $M$; note that the congruence modulo $M$ is $d'\equiv d$, not $d'\equiv d^{-1}$. It is used in the construction of an automorphism of the base-changed function field of $X_1(Mp)$ carrying prescribed relations with the $j$-invariant, the diamond operators and the Galois action.
